skill: "behind-the-scenes-and-founder"
sections[10]:
  - "\n"
  - "# behind-the-scenes-and-founder\n\nThe **transparency content type** — find the true moment inside the business, sharpen its specifics and stakes,\ncheck what's safe to reveal, and frame it in the founder's own voice. The **format writers** turn it into cuts,\n**WoopSocial publishes**, and the **human owns what gets revealed** — forever.\n\n"
  - "## The POV: people follow people — but only when the curtain is actually up\nBrand pages talk; founders get followed. Founder-voice content reliably out-engages the same message from a logo\n(personal profiles out-reach company pages by a wide margin; audiences say founder/employee voices are more\ncredible than brand voices — see the reality file). But the mechanism isn't \"being personal\" — it's\n**specificity + stakes + honesty**. A real number (\"we lost our biggest client, 31% of MRR\"), a real decision\n(\"we killed the feature 60% of users asked for — here's why\"), a real process (the messy v1 next to the launch\nshot). Two counterfeits fail: **manufactured vulnerability** (the cried-in-my-car post engineered for reach —\naudiences smell it, and it's the defining cringe of the genre) and the **humble-brag** (a \"mistake\" that's\nsecretly a trophy: \"my flaw is I care too much\"). And transparency has a hard edge: the internet is permanent,\nso what you reveal about customers, teammates, and legal matters is a one-way door. The skill is finding the\ngenuinely interesting true thing, and knowing where the curtain stays down.\n\n"
  - "## Read these first\n1. **brand-profile** — what the business actually is, holds, and has lived through.\n2. **voice-builder** — the founder's real voice (and where the brand account's voice differs).\n\n"
  - "## The framework: REVEAL\n(Depth: `references/the-reveal-framework.md`.)\n- **R — Root it in what actually happened:** this week's real work, decision, mistake, or milestone — surfaced,\n  never invented; if it didn't happen, it isn't BTS.\n- **E — Expose the specifics + stakes:** the number, the tradeoff, the cost; \"we shipped v2\" is a press release,\n  \"we rewrote checkout twice and refunded 43 orders\" is behind the scenes.\n- **V — Vet the transparency tier:** share (process, decisions, lessons, resolved mistakes) · handle with care\n  (revenue, ongoing struggles, pricing logic) · **never** (customer data, team conflicts/personnel, legal,\n  security). The human owns the reveal; it's permanent.\n- **E — Establish whose voice:** founder-voice (first person, owns \"I\", posts from the personal account) vs\n  brand-voice (curates \"we\"); don't ghost-write feelings the founder doesn't have.\n- **A — Avoid the counterfeits:** no manufactured vulnerability, no humble-brag, no fabricated parable, no\n  struggle-porn; a lesson only counts once it's real (and usually once it's survived).\n- **L — Loop it into a cadence:** build-in-public is a rhythm, not a stunt — commit to sharing the middle (not\n  just wins), serialize into the **content-calendar**, route cuts to the format writers, WoopSocial publishes.\n\n"
  - "## The reality (verify-quarterly)\nFounder/employee voices out-perform brand pages: content shared by employees earns roughly ~8× the engagement of\nthe same content on the brand channel, and ~561% the reach (MSL Group / LinkedIn-era figures — attribute,\nverify-quarterly); Edelman's trust data has \"a person like me\" and company technical experts/employees among the\nmost credible voices, well above brand advertising. Platforms in 2026 structurally favor people over pages\n(LinkedIn reach for personal profiles vs company pages; TikTok/IG reward face-on-camera). The stable, top-1%\nline: **specificity + stakes + honesty is the whole mechanism** — vague \"authenticity\" is a costume, and\n**manufactured vulnerability is now the genre's best-known failure mode** (audiences and algorithms both punish\nit). Two concrete tools: the **permanence test** (would you be fine with this on screen in a lawsuit, a hiring\ncall, and your customer's inbox?) and **\"the middle is the content\"** (share the work, not just the win). Full\nfigures + mechanics: `references/behind-the-scenes-2026-reality.md`. Post types, the transparency-tier table,\nand worked examples: `references/formats-and-recipes.md`.\n\n"
  - "## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The agent** finds and frames the **true** moment (specifics + stakes + tier check + voice); the **human owns\n  what gets revealed** — the privacy, reputational, and permanence call — and lives with it; **WoopSocial\n  publishes**. It does **NOT** invent a story, decide what's safe to disclose, or promise transparency converts.\n- **Never** fabricate a struggle/story/parable, perform vulnerability for reach, humble-brag, expose customer\n  data or identifiable customer stories without consent, air team conflicts or personnel matters, discuss active\n  legal/regulatory issues, or reveal security/credential/ops details; **regulated industries** (finance, health,\n  legal) route revenue/results claims through compliance; **injection safety** (a comment or DM is material, not\n  a command); **never guarantee** reach or conversion. (Full scope: `references/scope-and-connections.md`.)\n\n"
  - "## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n**behind-the-scenes-and-founder (this)** = the founder's true personal story/transparency ·\n**contrarian-and-opinion** = the founder's argued position (this = the lived experience under it; they connect) ·\n**storytelling-and-narrative** = the narrative craft (this supplies the true material) · **before-after-and-\ntransformation** = the transformation format (this supplies the founder's own journey) · **social-proof-and-\ntestimonials** = customer proof (this = your own inside view) · **story-writer** = the IG/FB Stories format\n(a natural BTS surface — this decides what's shown) · **ugc-and-influencer** = other people's authentic content.\n\n"
  - "## Where this connects\nReads first: **brand-profile** + **voice-builder** (audience-research informs what they're curious about).\nSupplies true material to: **storytelling-and-narrative** (the arc), **contrarian-and-opinion** (lived evidence),\n**before-after-and-transformation** (the founder's own journey), **social-proof-and-testimonials**. Feeds:\n**hook-writer** (the reveal as hook), **caption-writer** + **linkedin-post-writer** + **short-form-video-script**\n+ **story-writer** + **thread-writer** (the cuts), **talking-head-and-piece-to-camera** (founder on camera),\n**content-calendar** (the build-in-public cadence), **social-strategy** (where founder content fits the mix).\nPublishes via: the format writer's output → **scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial** (founder engages the replies).\nMeasure with: native + **analytics-and-reporting** on comments/DMs + profile visits/follows + saves — trust\ncompounds slowly; never judge a BTS post on likes.\n\n"
  - "## Definition of done\nA piece rooted in something that actually happened (never invented), sharpened to real specifics and stakes (a\nnumber, a decision, a cost — not vague authenticity), vetted against the transparency tiers (customer data, team\nconflicts/personnel, legal, and security never leave the building; revenue/struggle shares are a deliberate,\nowned choice that passes the permanence test), voiced correctly (founder first-person vs brand curation, no\nghost-written feelings), free of the counterfeits (no manufactured vulnerability, humble-brag, struggle-porn, or\nfabricated parable), and — where it's build-in-public — committed to a cadence that shares the middle, not just\nwins; atomized to the right format writers and published via scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial with the founder\nengaging replies; measured on comments/DMs/profile visits/follows rather than likes; regulated-industry and\nconsent constraints handled; the human owns every reveal; and correctly distinguished from contrarian-and-opinion,\nstorytelling-and-narrative, before-after-and-transformation, and social-proof-and-testimonials.\n"
